Smart Household Electricity Consumption Prediction Using Machine Learning

1. Project Overview
This project predicts household electricity consumption using historical electricity data and Machine Learning algorithms.
The main goal is to understand electricity usage patterns and help households manage their electricity consumption.
2. Problem Statement
Household electricity consumption changes depending on time and usage patterns. This project uses Machine Learning to predict electricity consumption based on previous readings and electrical measurements.
3. Objectives
- Predict household electricity consumption.
- Analyze electricity usage patterns.
- Identify high-consumption periods.
- Help households manage electricity usage.

4. Dataset
- Original records: 260,640
- Records after preprocessing: 255,429
- Target variable: Global Active Power (kW)
- Dataset frequency: Minute-level readings.
- Dataset period: January 2007 to June 2007.

5. Technologies Used
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- XGBoost
- Streamlit

6. Data Preprocessing
- Handled missing values.
- Removed duplicate records.
- Converted data types.
- Sorted records chronologically.
- Created lag and rolling mean features.
- Applied One-Hot Encoding.
- Applied StandardScaler.
- Split data into 80% training and 20% testing.

7. Machine Learning Algorithms
- Linear Regression
- Decision Tree Regressor
- Random Forest Regressor
- SGD Regressor
- Gradient Boosting Regressor
- XGBoost Regressor
8. Model Evaluation
The XGBoost model achieved the following test results:

| Metric | Result |
| R² Score | 0.957 |
| RMSE | 0.202 |
| MAE | 0.080 |

XGBoost was selected as the final model based on its performance.

9. Deployment
The project uses Streamlit to create a simple web application.
The application displays predicted electricity consumption and estimated usage information.

10. Conclusion
This project demonstrates how Machine Learning can be used to predict household electricity consumption and understand usage patterns.

